      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:177:1",
      "text": [
        " الْكَسِيرُ وَ الْمَبْطُونُ يُرْمَى عَنْهُمَا قَالَ وَ الصِّبْيَانُ يُرْمَى عَنْهُمْ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Muawiya Bin Ammar, and Abdul Rahman Bin Al Hajjaj, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The disabled, and the one with stomach illness, (the <span class=\"iTxt\">Jamarah</span>) would be pelted on both their behalf’. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘And the children, (the <span class=\"iTxt\">Jamarah</span>) would be pelted on their behalf’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "1. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Mu‘awiyah ibn ‘Ammar and ‘ Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hajjaj who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘It is permissible to throw pebbles on behalf of one who has a broken part or has stomach illness and so also is the rule about children.’” "
        ]
      }
